## How (lab standards apply)
This is a Raredon Lab project. Follow the lab **coding-standards** and
**github-standards** skills (Computational Manual Ch. 03–04):
- Scripts carry the standard header block; one coherent operation each; paths
  declared at top as named variables; no hardcoded values.
- Helpers (>~25 lines or reused) live in `functions/`, documented and parameterized.
- Narrated analysis is Quarto/Rmarkdown -> HTML in `docs/`.
- Files named `NN_YYYYMMDD_AB_descriptive-name.ext`.
- Fork model: push to your personal fork `dev`; PR to `RaredonLab/<name>` `dev`;
  never `main`. End-of-day push is mandatory.
- Data is described, never uploaded; code is written to run locally and save to
  disk. See manual Ch. 05–06.

